{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "2d2285df-a008-4908-aba4-6b4c89a4d395",
    "name": "allianz-vpc-provisioner",
    "description": "Serverless VPC provisioning API.\n\n1. Set the collection variable `password` to the output of `make demo-password`.\n2. Run any request. A pre-request script signs in to Cognito when `idToken` is empty.\n\nRun the whole collection in order: Auth, VPCs (create/get/list), Edge cases (every error code, overlap uses the VPC just created), Cleanup (delete). The CI deploy job runs it with newman after every deploy.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "id": "a5be52f9-b024-486b-90bd-6b92cbaabb8c",
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "25d565ab-3afe-467e-af93-a87b92abc071",
          "name": "Sign in (Cognito)",
          "request": {
            "description": "Exchanges the demo user's password for a Cognito ID token and stores it in {{idToken}}. Runs automatically before any other request when {{idToken}} is empty.",
            "url": "https://cognito-idp.{{region}}.amazonaws.com",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-amz-json-1.1"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Amz-Target",
                "value": "AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.InitiateAuth"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"AuthFlow\": \"USER_PASSWORD_AUTH\",\n  \"ClientId\": \"{{userPoolClientId}}\",\n  \"AuthParameters\": {\n    \"USERNAME\": \"{{username}}\",\n    \"PASSWORD\": \"{{password}}\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth",
              "noauth": []
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "id": "03dd6324-f2c6-4665-9df5-9c009345e595",
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('signed in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('idToken', pm.response.json().AuthenticationResult.IdToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "event": []
    },
    {
      "id": "208d2f4b-affc-474e-afb3-b68435c44298",
      "name": "VPCs",
      "item": [
        {
          "id": "eae7de49-0ef5-42e8-a01e-e4d6528dbae2",
          "name": "Create VPC",
          "request": {
            "description": "Creates a VPC with two subnets. Stores the returned id in {{vpcId}}.",
            "url": "{{apiEndpoint}}/vpcs",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "method": "POST",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"sandbox-vpc\",\n  \"cidr_block\": \"10.20.0.0/16\",\n  \"subnets\": [\n    {\n      \"cidr_block\": \"10.20.1.0/24\",\n      \"availability_zone\": \"us-east-1a\",\n      \"name\": \"public-web\",\n      \"is_public\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"cidr_block\": \"10.20.2.0/24\",\n      \"name\": \"private-app\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tags\": {\n    \"CostCenter\": \"R&D\"\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "id": "cc3c3687-a834-4f41-8a95-d8e69da273ba",
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('vpcId', d.vpc_id);",
                  "pm.test('AWS vpc id returned', () => pm.expect(d.aws_vpc_id).to.match(/^vpc-/));",
                  "pm.test('status ACTIVE', () => pm.expect(d.status).to.eql('ACTIVE'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "a3c6dae1-16eb-4869-8c45-0024848693c8",
          "name": "Get VPC",
          "request": {
            "description": "",
            "url": "{{apiEndpoint}}/vpcs/{{vpcId}}",
            "method": "GET"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "id": "4b95acd2-bc08-4444-aa64-b7d107573977",
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('same id', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.vpc_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('vpcId')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b263ebc2-ebf7-42dd-b191-df47eca58263",
          "name": "List my VPCs",
          "request": {
            "description": "",
            "url": "{{apiEndpoint}}/vpcs?scope=mine&limit=25",
            "method": "GET"
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "id": "627ec7bf-0dc1-4bbd-800f-1f3107b939c6",
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('contains created vpc', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().data.map(v => v.vpc_id)).to.include(pm.collectionVariables.get('vpcId')));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "73d0c952-5f0e-48de-a8df-98d1a1c9bda3",
          "name": "List all VPCs",
